+# Work Summary — 2026-03-02
+
+## Goal
+Stabilize DigiRig RX transcription and enable accurate fallback when OpenAI Realtime STT produces garbled/partial transcripts.
+
+## Key Changes Implemented
+- **Local Whisper fallback** on RX end (optional / conditional):
+  - Buffer RX PCM during active speech.
+  - On RX end, run local `whisper` CLI on a temp WAV.
+  - Use Whisper transcript when realtime transcript is missing/garbled (or always, if configured).
+- **Config additions** for local Whisper:
+  - `channels.digirig.stt.localWhisper.{enabled,alwaysUse,model,command,args,timeoutMs}`
+- **Runtime flow updates**:
+  - Capture PCM frames during RX.
+  - Decide between realtime transcript and Whisper fallback.
+  - Log selected transcript source (`openai-realtime` vs `local-whisper`).
+- **Docs + tests** updated for new options.
+
+## Intended Outcomes / Requirements
+- Improve transcription accuracy for RF audio without abandoning realtime RX.
+- Keep fast turn boundaries (Realtime VAD), but correct text using local Whisper.
+- Allow user to force Whisper if realtime remains unreliable.
+
+## Important Observation / Hypothesis
+> Rich believes the failing path was connecting DigiRig **PCM audio** to the **μ-law audio** path in voice-calls.
+
+This fallback addresses transcription accuracy while preserving realtime boundaries.
+
+## Tradeoffs
+- Local Whisper adds latency (seconds) and local CPU load.
+- Requires `whisper` CLI installed and accessible on PATH.
+- Realtime still determines RX start/stop.
+
+## Diff Summary (high level)
+- `src/runtime.ts`: RX PCM buffering, Whisper fallback, WAV writing & resampling helpers.
+- `src/config.ts` / `src/defaults.ts` / `src/config.test.ts`: new config schema + defaults.
+- `README.md`: new usage section for Whisper fallback.
+- `docs/digirig-whisper-fallback.md`: design + flow + tradeoffs.
+
+## Next Steps
+- Enable `stt.localWhisper.enabled` in config and re-test RF RX.
+- Tune `alwaysUse` if realtime remains unreliable.
